# Ticket 2 — VPN Connection Failure

## Issue
User reported being unable to connect to the company VPN.

## User Impact
The user was unable to establish a VPN connection to access company resources remotely.

## Troubleshooting Performed

Confirmed the user had working internet access.
Confirmed the VPN had worked previously.
Checked the Cisco Secure Client.
Verified the Cisco VPN service was running.
Checked Windows Firewall status.
Checked network adapters for errors.
Confirmed the Cisco Secure Client virtual adapter was present.
Checked the VPN client logs.
Ran network troubleshooting commands:
  - `ipconfig /all`
  - `ping vpn.company.local`
  - `nslookup vpn.company.local`
Confirmed the VPN hostname could not be resolved.
Restarted the workstation and retested the VPN.

## Findings

The workstation was unable to resolve the internal VPN hostname. The Cisco Secure Client service and virtual network adapter were functioning normally.
The issue required further investigation of the company's VPN/DNS configuration.

## Resolution
The issue was documented and ecalated to the appropriate Network/VPN support team.

